BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Insect Pinning Class: Hewitson's Olivewing Butterfly
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17671968@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:What's cooler than a snazzy-looking butterfly? Easy. A butterf
 ly with two snazzy-looking sides. The Hewitson's Olivewing Butterfly is ex
 actly that. So much so that deciding which way you want to display it is g
 oing to be one of those quandaries you'll puzzle over until smoke is pouri
 ng from your ears.\n\nPro tip: Each side makes a rad display\, so don't hu
 rt yourself trying to decide which is the best side like we did.\nAll of i
 ts glamour isn't strictly for appearance\, though. Like all creatures of t
 he natural world\, there's a rhyme and reason behind its look. With its wi
 ngs closed\, the underside looks just like a dead leaf\, complete with ear
 thy browns\, leaf-like veins\, and mottled patterns. This little trick is 
 called cryptic coloration. Rather than trying to scare predators or advert
 ise toxicity\, it simply disappears into the background by looking exactly
  like something predators ignore every day: a dead leaf. It's one of those
  butterflies that's surprisingly difficult to spot in the wild until it mo
 ves.\n\nFor us\, that's pretty annoying when trying to spot them while tro
 mping through the rainforests of Central and South America\, but for them\
 , it's a blessing. Over millions of years\, evolution has decided who gets
  to stick around and who goes the way of the dodo (although that's not ent
 irely the dodo's fault). The Hewitson's Olivewing Butterfly is a product o
 f that evolutionary process. The butterflies that could blend in and avoid
  the attention of predators were the butterflies...\n\n$110\, 18+ or with 
 Guardian\nPaxton Gate's\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/
 insect-pinning-class-hewitson-s-olivewing-butterfly-tickets\nSource: DoThe
 Bay
GEO:37.7596242;-122.4217046
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33616544/254659ef-a121-432f-836c-1ddefcd5ab0c.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Paxton Gate\, 824 Valencia Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/4/insect-pinning-class-hewitson-s-
 olivewing-butterfly-tickets
END:VEVENT
