 :\n\n- Dinner by Chef Reem Assil of Reem's California\n- Small bites and d
 esserts from Executive Chef Lorenzo Caamal\, Merkado\n- Cocktails by Merka
 do\n- Live music and performances from Melissa Cruz\, Zedan & Osman\, and 
 Diana Gameros featuring Raúl Vargas on cajón\n- Thoughtful programming\n
 - Our first-ever Spicy Soiree market featuring vendors\, makers\, and arti
 sts\n\nNo Immigrants No Spice (NINS) is known for BBQ Without Borders\, br
 inging hundreds of people together around food. The Spicy Soiree will be a
  bit different - a more intimate gathering designed to spark connection an
 d conversation around the table\, while raising funds for the NINS mission
  of shifting the narrative on immigration\, and making the 2027 BBQ Withou
 t Borders event possible.\n\nNote: we are offering a reduced price “ente
 rtainment-only” ticket to expand access to this event.\nThis is a limite
 d-capacity event and we expect it to sell out. Get your tickets before the
 y're gone!\n____________________________\n\nAbout Chef Reem Assil\nReem As
 sil is an award-winning Palestinian-Syrian chef based in Oakland\, Califor
 nia\, working at the intersection of food\, community\, and social justice
 . Reem is the owner and founder of nationally-acclaimed Arab restaurant an
 d bakery Reem’s California. Reem is a James Beard Award Finalist for Out
