BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Science Scoop: Holly Ingraham
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17754876@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:The Science Scoop\nPlease join us for the next session of The 
 Science Scoop\, a quarterly public lecture series hosted by UCSF Basic Sci
 ences. Discovery for ALL!\n\nWe invite you to learn about how curiosity-dr
 iven research is leading to critical medical advances. Through engaging le
 ctures geared towards a lay audience\, premier researchers at the Universi
 ty of California\, San Francisco will share the challenges and joys of mak
 ing scientific discoveries and their impact on bettering human health. The
  audience will have the opportunity to ask questions at the end of the tal
 k.\n\nThis is a FREE lecture open to the general public\, and all are welc
 ome. No tickets or registration needed.\n\nThe Talk\n\nHow Science Can Imp
 rove Health for Women … and Men\n\nThe Speaker\nHolly A. Ingraham\, PhD\
 , is the Herzstein Professor of Molecular Physiology at the University of 
 California\, San Francisco. Her research focuses on hormone-responsive nod
 es in the brain and peripheral tissues that impact metabolic\, skeletal\, 
 and gut physiology and women’s health. Through question-driven basic sci
 ence\, Ingraham has uncovered how hormonal fluctuations lead to adaptive r
 esponses in females across their lifespan. Ingraham is an elected fellow o
 f the American Association for the Advancement of Science and a member of 
 the National Academy of Sciences and the American Academy of Arts and Scie
 nces. She earned her Ph.D. from UCSD.\nhttps://ingrahamlab.ucsf.edu/\n\nIf
  you would like to receive email updates and invitations rela...\n\nFree\n
 UCSF BASIC SCIENCES PRESENTS\n\nTickets: https://ucsfsciencescoop.eventbri
 te.com/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/14/the-science-scoop
 -holly-ingraham-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34011664/2b50d110-cfa2-4f23-8849-1256df66958e.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Byers Auditorium\, Genentech Hall\, 250 Campus Way\, San Francisc
 o\, CA\, 94158
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/14/the-science-scoop-holly-ingraha
 m-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Presentation: Why You Need More Wonder in Your Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17913965@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Discover simple ways to bring more wonder\, curiosity and magi
 c into everyday life with San Francisco illusionist Andrew Evans\, founder
  of The Magic Patio\, and writer Laura Holson\, founder of The Box Session
 s. Explore how cultivating a sense of wonder can support well-being\, redu
 ce stress and strengthen relationships\, while learning easy ways to incor
 porate more delight into daily life. The program concludes with a magic tr
 ick taught by Evans that everyone can use to entertain and amaze.\n\nThis 
 event is a collaboration with The Box Sessions\, a company founded by Hols
 on to inspire curiosity and personal creativity.\n\nAndrew Evans is the cr
 eator and founder of The Magic Patio\, a magic speakeasy tucked in a hidde
 n corner of San Francisco. A graduate of Stanford's product design program
 \, Evans incorporates the techniques he learned there to create magic. His
  reputation is building among the magic cognoscenti and he was recently fe
 atured on Penn and Teller: Fool Us\, the TV show created by the duo that i
 s the longest-running act in Las Vegas history.\n\nLaura Holson is an awar
 d-winning writer and visual journalist for The New York Times\, photograph
 er\, creativity advisor and teacher. Laura is a gifted storyteller and kee
 n observer of culture and human behavior. Nearly a decade ago\, Holson sta
 rted a creativity salon that became the foundation for The Box Sessions\, 
 which brings together film makers\, musicians\, writers\, storytellers and
  artists.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by San Francisco Public Libr...\n\nFree\nSa
 n Francisco Public Library\n\nTickets: https://sfpl.org/events/2026/10/14/
 presentation-why-you-need-more-wonder-your-life\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/10/14/presentation-why-you-need-more-wonder-in-your-life-
 tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34760145/50f29e14-e93e-4882-87bf-195c223e9872.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Koret Auditorium (SF Public Library)\, 100 Larkin St\, San Franci
 sco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/14/presentation-why-you-need-more-
 wonder-in-your-life-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Tenses + MSHR + Sung Kim
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17729682@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Variety
DESCRIPTION:Buy Tickets\n\nDoors 8pm / Show 8:30pm\n\n$17 / free or discou
 nted for members\n\nThe Tenses—comprised of Ju Suk Reet Meate and Oblivi
 a from Smegma\, the legendary “band without musicians” founded in 1973
 —held a tradition of weekly jam sessions with MSHR (Brenna Murphy & Birc
 h Cooper) beginning in 2012. The jam room AKA “Smegma Studios” AKA “
 purple planet room\,” was a longtime anchor of the Portland underground 
 music scene with a rotating cast of weirdos and noise musicians coming thr
 ough over the decades. Lifelong archivists\, The Tenses would record and c
 atalog every session\, occasionally releasing highlights on labels such as
  their own Pigface Records\, including a collaborative release with MSHR i
 n 2015.\n\nThe two duos converge for a rare west coast tour\, with The Ten
 ses’ collection of cassette recorders\, plastic water jugs\, pocket trum
 pet\, Ciat-Lonbarde synths\, and occasional surf rock riffs. MSHR’s new 
 work\, Negative Flower\, combines their signature physical controllers and
  light feedback with a digital system constructed in the SuperCollider pro
 gramming environment. Sung Kim joins for an opening set with his expertly 
 crafted handmade musical constructions drawing on kotos\, lap steel\, and 
 various other stringed instruments.\n\n$17\n\nTickets: https://link.dice.f
 m/d134351f31ae\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-tenses
 -mshr-sung-kim-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.765289;-122.418493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33891158/962642f4-79da-4293-9f55-7d93aa34db3a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:The Lab\, 2948 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-tenses-mshr-sung-kim-ticket
 s
END:VEVENT
