SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Activism
DESCRIPTION:The Clift Royal Sonesta Hotel\, a San Francisco landmark since
  1915\, continues its monthly speaker series\, Making History Fun Again\, 
 designed to celebrate the city’s legendary past through lively storytell
 ing\, fascinating personalities and unforgettable local history.\nOn Thurs
 day\, October 15\, award-winning arts and culture journalist Rae Alexandra
  will present “Unsung Heroines: The Women Who Changed the Bay Area\,” 
 a spirited journey through the lives of 35 remarkable women whose courage\
 , creativity and determination helped shape San Francisco and Northern Cal
 ifornia.\nDrawn from Alexandra’s long-running KQED series Rebel Girls Fr
 om Bay Area History\, her book\, Unsung Heroines: 35 Women Who Changed the
  Bay Area (published by City Lights and available in bookstores all over N
 orthern California)\, restores an extraordinary and diverse group of women
  to their rightful place in the region’s story. Their lives span the ear
 liest years of San Francisco and the greater Bay Area through the present 
 day.\nEducators and organizers\, adventurers and entertainers\, activists 
 and innovators\, the women in Unsung Heroines challenged convention\, tran
 sformed their communities and opened paths for generations that followed. 
 Together\, their stories offer a vivid new rendering of Northern Californi
 a history—one told through women whose influence has too often been over
 looked.\nDuring the program\, Alexandra will share some of the surprising 
 personalities and discoveries behind the book\, explore why these s...\n\n
 Free\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-clift-royal-so
 nesta-hotel-continues-its-speaker-series-making-history-fun-again-tickets\
 nSource: DoTheBay
