CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:Remember last year when the San Francisco Board of Supervisors
  officially declared October 17th as Broke-Ass Stuart Day? Yeah\, that was
  pretty cool.\n\nAnd the party that we threw was epic!\n\nWell\, we’ve d
 ecided to make it a yearly event and this time we’re teaming up with the
  folks over at the Clement Street Art Fair to do something truly wonderful
 .\nClement St. Art Fair & Broke-Ass Stuart Day\n\nI’m joining forces wit
 h The Clement Street Merchants Association and WorkshopSF for the 2nd Annu
 al Broke-Ass Stuart Day and the 3rd annual Clement Street Art Fair.\n\nRSV
 P Right Here!\n\nClement Street – from 6th to 8th Avenues – will close
  to traffic to provide a fun-filled day of art activations\, live music\, 
 local makers\, and community building. The event will be hosted by Clement
  Street Merchants Association and I will emcee!\n\nIt’s all going down o
 n October 17th from 12:00 PM to 5:00 PM and will offer a ton of fun activi
 ties for people of all ages:\nMusical Performances:\n\nSweet Lew\n\nPlovve
 r\n\nSWISS.\n\nEmily Afton\n\nArtist Activations:\n\nMake-and-take crafts 
 by Workshop SF\n\nDIY Postcards & Love Letters to Clement by Risa Iwasaki 
 Culbertson and Leah Jachimowicz of Coffee n Cream Press\n\nLive screen pri
 nting by Fleetwood\n\nCommunity Art Project by Kate Campbell\n\nFeatured A
 rtist:\n\nHollis Callas (Designed SF's "I Voted!" stickers and this year
 ’s poster)\n\nPlus there will be food\, drinks\, activities for the kids
  and even a bike fix-it station by Scenic Routes.\n\nSo come out on Saturd
 ay October 17th\, brin...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://brokeassstuart.com/p
 /the-2nd-annual-bas-day-is-an-art-fair\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/even
 ts/2026/10/17/broke-ass-stuart-day-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
