BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Litquake Presents Menopause Extravaganza: The Science and Culture 
 of a Subject No One Used to Want to Talk About
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T163000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17794224@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:The Arts
DESCRIPTION:Menopause Extravaganza: The Science and Culture of a Subject N
 o One Used to Want to Talk About\n\nSunday\, October 18\, 2026\n\nDoors: 2
 :30 PM\n\nAll Ages\n\nSeated event\n\nView our FAQ page for more info\, or
  contact us at [email protected] with any accommodation requests.\n\nMenop
 ause\, a natural consequence of aging\, has for centuries been alternately
  ignored and belittled\, seen mostly through a male lens of bafflement\, r
 epugnance\, and boilerplate misogyny. Now\, however\, a growing body of wo
 men and their doctors are rejecting this traditional view\, developing new
  therapies and strategies as well as ways to appreciate the new freedoms i
 t can offer.\n\nThis energizing (and overdue) afternoon features Dr. Louan
 n Brizendine\, author of The Female Brain\, reading from her forthcoming Y
 our Brain on Menopause and joining other panelists in a conversation led b
 y Keli Dailey: Dr. Sarah Isquick (a colleague of Dr. Sally Greenwald\, fea
 tured in the recent New Yorker article “The Billionaires’ Vagina Club
 ”)\, psychiatrist Dr. Alecia Greenlee\, and menopause doula Lasara Firef
 ox Allen\, author of Genderqueer Menopause.\n\nSelect performers from The 
 Menopause Monologues® will kick off the event. Bring your friends for a c
 onversation-sparking afternoon.\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/20
 26/10/18/litquake-presents-menopause-extravaganza-the-science-and-culture-
 of-a-subject-no-one-used-to-want-to-talk-about-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7544054;-122.4183493
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34194924/c8942b2c-ff71-41d4-aa42-b4ace19e22e4.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Gray Area\, 2665 Mission Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/litquake-presents-menopause-ext
 ravaganza-the-science-and-culture-of-a-subject-no-one-used-to-want-to-talk
 -about-tickets
END:VEVENT
